---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---
<DocsLayout title="Agent Status Monitoring — Band Docs">
  <h1>Agent Status Monitoring</h1>
  <p>
    Band continuously monitors the status of coding agents running in your worktrees. Agent
    status is displayed as a colored indicator dot on each worktree card, giving you an
    at-a-glance view of what every agent is doing across all your repos.
  </p>

  <h2>Status Types</h2>
  <p>
    Each worktree's coding agent can be in one of these states:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Idle (no indicator)</strong> &mdash; Nothing is running. A turn you stopped also
      shows no indicator.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Working (yellow dot)</strong> &mdash; The agent is executing a task: reading files,
      writing code or running commands.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Monitoring (yellow ring)</strong> &mdash; The turn is over but a loop, a cron job
      or a background command is still running.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Question (amber "?")</strong> &mdash; The agent waits for your answer: a
      permission request, <code>AskUserQuestion</code> or <code>ExitPlanMode</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Done (green dot)</strong> &mdash; The agent finished its turn. Opening the
      worktree sets it back to idle.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Failed (red dot)</strong> &mdash; The turn ended in an error, a refusal or a
      limit. Opening the worktree sets it back to idle.
    </li>
  </ul>

