  <h2>How Status Is Detected</h2>
  <p>
    Band detects agent status through <strong>Claude Code hooks</strong>. When the Band dashboard
    installs hooks (prompted on first launch), it registers hook handlers that fire on key
    Claude Code lifecycle events.
  </p>
  <p>
    The hooks use the <code>band notify</code> command to send status updates to the Band server:
  </p>
  <pre><code set:html={`echo '{"hook_event_name":"Stop","cwd":"/path/to/worktree"}' | band notify`}></code></pre>
  <p>
    The <code>band notify</code> command is agent-agnostic: it simply forwards the raw hook
    payload (plus the working directory) to the Band server. The server resolves which
    worktree the directory belongs to, then dispatches to that worktree's coding-agent
    adapter to translate the payload into a status — so the event→status mapping lives next
    to each agent's logic and adding a new agent never requires changing the CLI. The
    resulting status change is broadcast to the dashboard in real-time via server-sent
    events (SSE).
  </p>

  <h3>Hook Events</h3>
  <p>
    Chats in Band report their state through the Agent Client Protocol and need no hooks. Claude
    Code in a terminal reports through hooks, which you install yourself: Band shows a banner
    when a host has Claude Code and no hooks, and <strong>Settings &gt; Agent hooks</strong>
    installs, reinstalls or removes them per host. Band never edits
    <code>~/.claude/settings.json</code> on its own, and Remove deletes only Band's entries. Each
    hook ends with <code>&gt;/dev/null 2&gt;&amp;1 || true</code>, runs in the background and
    always exits 0, so a hook can never interrupt your agent.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>UserPromptSubmit, PreToolUse, PostToolUse, PostToolUseFailure</strong> &mdash; <em>working</em>. <code>PreToolUse</code> for <code>AskUserQuestion</code> or <code>ExitPlanMode</code> is a <em>question</em>.</li>
    <li><strong>PermissionRequest</strong> &mdash; <em>question</em>, for every tool.</li>
    <li><strong>Stop</strong> &mdash; <em>done</em>, or <em>monitoring</em> while <code>session_crons</code> or <code>background_tasks</code> show work that outlives the turn.</li>
    <li><strong>StopFailure</strong> &mdash; <em>failed</em>.</li>
    <li><strong>SubagentStart, SubagentStop</strong> &mdash; the session stays <em>working</em> while subagents run after the main turn.</li>
    <li><strong>PostCompact</strong> &mdash; a manual <code>/compact</code> is <em>done</em>.</li>
    <li><strong>SessionEnd</strong> &mdash; the session stops counting.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Status Display</h2>
  <p>
    Agent status is displayed in two locations:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Worktree list</strong> &mdash; A small colored dot appears next to the branch name in the repo list. This is always visible and provides a quick summary.</li>
    <li><strong>Worktree detail view</strong> &mdash; When viewing a worktree in the web interface, the status is shown alongside other worktree metadata.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Notification Sounds</h2>
  <p>
    Band can play a notification sound when an agent asks a question, finishes or fails.
    <em>Monitoring</em> is silent. This is useful when you have multiple agents running and want
    to know when one finishes without constantly watching the dashboard.
  </p>
  <p>
    To enable notification sounds, go to <a href="/docs/settings">Settings</a> and toggle
    <strong>Notification sound</strong> on. You can choose from several built-in sounds and
    preview them before saving.
  </p>

  <h2>Installing Hooks</h2>
  <p>
    If Claude Code hooks are not installed, the dashboard shows a setup prompt at the bottom:
  </p>
  <pre><code>Install Claude Code hooks for agent status detection  [Install]</code></pre>
  <p>
    Click <strong>Install</strong> to set up the hooks. This configures Claude Code to send
    lifecycle notifications to Band automatically. The hooks are installed globally and apply
    to all Claude Code sessions on your machine.
  </p>

  <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>No status showing</strong> &mdash; Make sure Claude Code hooks are installed
      (check the dashboard for the install prompt). Verify the Band server is running.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Status stuck on "working"</strong> &mdash; This can happen if the agent process
      was terminated without sending a stop notification. Restarting the agent or creating a
      new task will reset the status.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Hooks prompt keeps appearing</strong> &mdash; Another tool may be overwriting
      the Claude Code hooks configuration. Check your Claude Code settings for conflicting
      hook definitions.
    </li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
